---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import { site } from '../../content/site'
import portrait from '../../assets/photos/ryan-amarit.webp'
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Ryan Amarit is a web lead and product engineer in Fort Worth, Texas, with nine years of building websites, design systems and products."
  palette="about"
>
  <section class="wrap page-hero" data-section="about" data-gl="page">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="page-title" data-split>Strategy to shipped code.</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:2rem">{site.intro}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap about-grid" data-section="about-body">
    <div class="portrait">
      <Image
        src={portrait}
        alt="Ryan Amarit"
        width={1280}
        widths={[480, 720, 960, 1280]}
        sizes="(min-width: 900px) 42vw, 100vw"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="prose-lg">
      <p>
        I have been building for the web for nine years, in-house and at an agency, with a graduate
        certificate in computer science from Seattle University.
      </p>
      <p>
        Today I am the Web Development Tech Lead at 8am (formerly AffiniPay). I lead the platform
        behind eight brand websites, the Tailwind and Storybook design system they share, and the
        Contentful tools content teams publish with. I set the web team's priorities with Marketing,
        Growth, Design, Brand and Content, and I lead one other developer.
      </p>
      <p>
        I care about the whole job, not one slice of it. The plan has to serve the business, the page
        has to be fast and easy to read, the code has to be something a team can maintain, and it all
        has to work for someone on a phone with a screen reader and reduced motion on.
      </p>
      <p>
        Away from work I build side projects, including RulerIQ, a pre-launch SaaS that shows brands
        which pages AI assistants cite.
      </p>

      <dl class="facts">
        {site.facts.map((fact) => (
          <div>
            <dt>{fact.label}</dt>
            <dd>{fact.value}</dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>

      <p style="margin-top:2.5rem">
        <a class="btn btn-accent" href="/projects/">See the work</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
